[Music]  hey everyone and welcome back to the  playstation competition center and our  coverage of tekken 7.  i'm mark van and i'm here with riff and  today we're going to talk to you about  the rage system  exactly rage is a mechanic that gives  you more power when you're closer to  being ko so let's quickly take a look at  that  in tekken 7 your health are split into  two colors about 80  one color and 20 another color when you  take enough damage and are at about 20  health you will hear a special sound  effect and the health bar's border  starts to flash red  your character is now enraged and all  your attacks will do increased damage  this is of course very useful in itself  especially if you have to make  a big comeback but there's more once you  have rage available  you get access to two entirely new moves  these are called  rage drives and rage arts the rage drive  is an entirely new move only accessible  while in rage  when one is performed the camera will  shift and the character will flash blue  each character's rage drive is unique  there are commonly very fast  flooding attacks that will lead to more  offense even if they're blocked  and if they hit they will lead to  massive damage they may even be used in  the middle of a combo to earn more  damage than what is normally possible  rage drives are very strong tools that  must be respected and will often make  the defender nervous when they're  opponents near ko  rage arts on the other hand are  cinematic super attacks that do a lot of  raw damage  importantly they have armor at the  beginning of the move which means you  can blow through an opponent's attack  however you still take damage from any  hit you armor through and this can ko  you  so they are less useful when you are  extremely low on health however  the lower your health bar the more  damage your weight charge will do  unlike rage drives if your opponent  anticipates your rage arc  most are easily blocked or avoided and  your opponent can punish you with a  counter attack so they are more often  used as a high damage  desperation move or as a combo finisher  once you use your rage driver rage art  you no longer have access to the passive  damage boost  and you can no longer do another rage  art or rage drive for the rest of the  round  so if you have to make a comeback you  have to make sure it counts otherwise  you lose the extra damage  it's important to make sure that you're  able to use it towards the end of the  round to make sure you actually  hail your opponent right and rage drives  and rage yards are very powerful tools  that you really don't want to forget  about when you're beginner player  and of course you know they're such a  big comeback mechanic that you really  have to kind of experiment with your  character to see which ones work best  for you  that's it for this episode this tutorial  was made in partnership with the  playstation competition center team  you can check out more at  compete.playstation.com  to watch learn and to compete subscribe  to the bne esports channel for more  tutorials  and tekken 7 content

